    "created_at": "2019-10-29T18:23:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-29T18:23:56Z",
    "body": "This makes sense to me. I wonder why this was originally written this way.\r\n\r\nThe only question in my mind is, whether we delete that row entirely, or keep it and change the \"DOM anchor\" column.\r\n\r\nI guess that comes down to whether area elements are [\"being rendered\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#being-rendered). If they are, then the first row of the table seems to be enough, and we should delete the row in question. If they are not, but instead the img element is being rendered with the area elements acting as hints of some kind, then we need to keep the row in the table.\r\n\r\nI guess I am leaning toward the interpretation that the area elements are not \"being rendered\". And also, it'd probably be clearer to just keep the row. But, I am curious what others think. Also, I wonder if there are other uses of \"being rendered\" in the spec that would allow us to actually test whether area elements count as being rendered or not, in some other fashion.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
